# Textarea

Use a textarea for a specific answer that needs several lines.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## When to use it

Use it for a dashboard description or a bounded household instruction. Set an initial height that matches the expected answer and allow the user to resize it vertically.

## When not to use it

Do not use an open box when a small set of structured choices would answer the question more reliably. Do not imply that a note is monitored by a support service.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Explain who can read a household note and where it appears. Do not store passwords, access tokens or private care instructions in a shared dashboard note. Preserve draft text through ordinary validation errors and make unsaved changes clear before navigating away.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use a visible label and short associated hint. Keep paste and browser editing shortcuts available. Do not impose a limit simply to control card height; use character count only for a justified storage or delivery restriction.

